  "experiment": "E8",
  "hidden_pattern": "IPC-2221's internal-layer rule is not an independent measurement: its k is halved (0.024 vs 0.048), which is exactly the same as halving the current. For a fixed current and temperature rise the internal area is therefore 2^(1/0.725)=2.60 times the external area by construction. The IPC-2152 empirical fit does not reproduce that penalty; at 10 A, 10 C, 1 oz it predicts 13.3 mm internal versus 15.2 mm external. For external traces the same fit is 2.1 times wider than IPC-2221 at 10 A, and a 2026 chart reading is 2.6 times wider, so IPC-2221 is non-conservative at high current by roughly a factor of 1.7-2.0 in current. At 1 A the two methods nearly agree, which is why the discrepancy is invisible in low-current examples. The chart and the fit differ by 23% at the 10 A case, so the absolute width carries a fit-versus-chart uncertainty that the paper reports rather than hides.",
